==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Germanic|knehtaz|lang=ang}}, of unknown origin: cognate with Old Frisian ''[[knecht]]'', Old Saxon ''[[knecht]]'', Old High German ''[[kneht]]'' (German ''[[Knecht]]'', Danish {{term|knægt}}, Dutch ''[[knecht]]'').

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/kniçt/|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|g=m}}

# [[boy]], [[youth]]
# (male) [[servant]], [[attendant]]
# male of high military rank, ranking below a [[baron]], usually previously having worked as a [[page]] or [[squire]]

====Declension====
{{ang-decl-noun-a-m|cniht}}

